<title>GERMANY: SOCCER-HUIBERTS QUITS MOENCHENGLADBACH FOR ALKMAAR.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-HUIBERTS QUITS MOENCHENGLADBACH FOR ALKMAAR.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch striker Max Huiberts has agreed to join Netherlands side AZ Alkmaar for around $260,000 after failing to establish himself at struggling German first division club Borussia Moenchengladbach.</p>
<p>The 25-year-old moved to Germany from Dutch club Roda Kerkrade last year for $780,000, but failed to score in 18 first team matches for Moenchengladbach.</p>
